### Root Cause
In [`ControlFlowAnalysis.computeFollowNode`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/closure_14_group_d_fix/src/com/google/javascript/jscomp/ControlFlowAnalysis.java#L764-L771), when control exits a `finally` block to transition to destination nodes stored in `finallyMap` (e.g. from an exception or early return within the `try` block), the edge was created as `Branch.UNCOND` instead of `Branch.ON_EX`. Because [`CheckMissingReturn`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/closure_14_group_d_fix/src/com/google/javascript/jscomp/CheckMissingReturn.java) considers `Branch.UNCOND` as normal execution flow, it treated the path exiting the `finally` block directly to the function exit as a normal code path that missed a return statement when taking the non-return branch of the `try` block.

### Fix
Changed the branch type from `Branch.UNCOND` to `Branch.ON_EX` when linking the `finally` block to nodes in `finallyMap` in [`ControlFlowAnalysis.java`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/closure_14_group_d_fix/src/com/google/javascript/jscomp/ControlFlowAnalysis.java#L767):
```diff
@@ -764,7 +764,7 @@ final class ControlFlowAnalysis implements Callback, CompilerPass {
         } else if (parent.getLastChild() == node){
           if (cfa != null) {
             for (Node finallyNode : cfa.finallyMap.get(parent)) {
-              cfa.createEdge(fromNode, Branch.UNCOND, finallyNode);
+              cfa.createEdge(fromNode, Branch.ON_EX, finallyNode);
             }
           }
           return computeFollowNode(fromNode, parent, cfa);
```

